+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+In confirmed MAIN standby, each fresh gas press of at least 0.1s and release requests one SET− press/release regardless of engagement or lateral activity. No extra release dwell or second press; actual stock ON stops remaining SET frames. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF, renewed gas, driver buttons, lost eligibility or cancellation interrupt input. Cancellation takes priority.
+
+Automatic SET uses only a newly observed CLU11 sample received within 8ms. Do not add a 10ms delay or remember a timing slot. Skip older samples and await the next within the original pedal/press deadlines, without extending their expiry.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Turn the setting ON, update/restart while parked with MAIN OFF, then press MAIN ON after boot. Initial MAIN OFF is independent of AutoEngage. Each qualified release permits one press; another needs three seconds after the last TX and a fresh pedal cycle. Blocked/expired cues are not queued. OFF or an unauthorized profile sends no automatic SET; OFF preserves MAIN tracking.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+One press is at most three frames/60ms followed by release. Existing Panda profile limits remain; the host does not schedule a second press. Retain 0.5s MAIN settling, initial target/dashboard 30–160km/h and existing input/driver-priority guards. The current automatic-SET profile also requires front-left and rear-right wheel speeds at 30–160km/h. Discard releases below that wheel floor even if the dashboard exceeds 30; a fresh pedal cycle is required after speed recovers. `sample_age_ms` and `late_samples` report sample age and late-sample count. Absolute MAIN state is not decoded; standby already ON at restart needs a MAIN-OFF restart or actual stock ON from physical SET for synchronization. TX echo is not ECU acceptance; no direct braking, standstill launch or vehicle acceptance guarantee is provided.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
